public <V, E> IsomorphicGraphMapping<V, E> identity(Graph<V, E> graph) {
    /*
     * Implementation note: an identity mapping is a mapping from graph to graph, where every vertex in the source graph
     * is mapped to the same vertex in the target graph. Likewise, every edge in the source graph is mapped to the same edge
     * in the target graph.
     *
     * In this case, we can simply use the same vertex and edge lists for both the source and target graphs, and the
     * resulting mapping will be an isomorphism.
     */
    return new IsomorphicGraphMapping<>(graph, graph);
}

